												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Coming Soon To Early Access</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">The developers of this game intend to release as a work in progress, developing with the feedback of players.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“Debauchery &amp; Magic is an ambitious open-world co-op ARPG with deep procedural systems, dungeons, professions, abilities, loot, economy, and more. Early Access allows us to launch the core gameplay loop early while continuing to refine systems that benefit most from community input. The game’s identity is shaped by player experimentation, feedback, and emergent play, so releasing in Early Access lets us iterate quickly, expand content, and fine-tune balance with real players involved.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“We expect Early Access to last around one year. During that time, we'll be delivering major content updates, polishing features, expanding world systems, and improving performance across all platforms.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“We plan for the full version to expand on the Early Access foundation. The current vision includes exploring additional zones and biomes, introducing new dungeon types, and potentially adding more professions with deeper ability paths. We're also experimenting with ideas for expanding crafting, alchemy, gambling, drinking, and other progression systems.<br />
<br />
As development continues, I expect to iterate on enemy variety, bosses, minibosses, world events, and co-op/social features. I also aim to keep improving performance, stability, and overall polish across supported platforms.<br />
<br />
These plans may evolve based on testing, resources, and community feedback. Early Access allows me to refine the direction of the game over time, and the final release will reflect what I'm able to build upon this foundation - guided by what players respond to during development.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“Debauchery &amp; Magic is currently in closed playtesting. Core systems are implemented and actively being refined as testers explore dungeons, professions, abilities, and early co-op features.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“Yes. The game will be cheaper during Early Access. As major features, zones, and systems are added, the price will increase to reflect the expanded scope and content.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“The community plays a central role in shaping Debauchery &amp; Magic. Feedback from closed playtesters, Early Access players, and the broader community will directly influence balance, content priorities, new professions, ability paths, dungeon features, and quality-of-life improvements. We’ll be maintaining active communication channels, pushing frequent updates, gathering feedback, and iterating rapidly based on how the player base interacts with the game.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
